<h2>Scenario 7: Picture Element with Multiple Sources</h2>

<p>Testing responsive picture element with multiple source options and fallback img element.</p>

<picture>
    <source media="(min-width: 800px)" srcset="https://picsum.photos/556/350?random=@(RandomPrefix)18" width="556" height="350" />
    <source media="(min-width: 400px)" srcset="https://picsum.photos/400/250?random=@(RandomPrefix)19" width="400" height="250" />
    <img class="image-left" src="https://picsum.photos/300/200?random=@(RandomPrefix)20" alt="Responsive picture element test" width="300" height="200" loading="@LoadingAttribute" />
</picture>

<p>The picture element provides responsive image delivery with multiple source options based on media queries. Text should wrap around the picture element similar to regular images. The browser selects the appropriate source based on viewport width: large screens get 556x350px, medium screens get 400x250px, and small screens get the fallback 300x200px image.</p>

<p>This scenario tests how the PhRichText component handles the picture element with its nested source elements and fallback img element, ensuring proper positioning and text flow behavior with responsive image delivery.</p>

<h2>Layout Reset Validation</h2>

<p>Final floating image to confirm layout reset after closing the rich text area.</p>

<img src="https://picsum.photos/300/300?random=@(RandomPrefix)17" alt="Final layout validation" class="image-left" width="300" height="300" loading="@LoadingAttribute" />

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// Controls whether images use lazy loading or eager loading.
    /// When true, images load lazily. When false, images load eagerly.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool LazyLoading { get; set; }

    private string LoadingAttribute => LazyLoading ? "lazy" : "eager";

    private string RandomPrefix => LazyLoading ? "2" : "1";
}